##errorCatcher Echo
##
## Fixed this session (beta report, Gert):
##  1. rainRateHourly chained .mm_per_hour onto .rain (group_rain, an
##     accumulated amount -- always mm, not a genuine rate type), which
##     threw KeyError: 'mm_per_hour' and crashed the ENTIRE template on
##     every generation cycle. Reverted to .mm, matching the alltime
##     "rainRate" key below it, which was already correct. hailRate-based
##     .mm_per_hour occurrences (prainRateHourly, prainRate) are genuinely
##     group_rainrate and are correct as-is -- left untouched.
##  2. This copy of the file had NO #try/#except crash guards anywhere
##     (an older/reverted copy predating that convention -- see the
##     handover doc's "File source-of-truth discipline" note). A single
##     unregistered observation type (e.g. a particulate sensor field not
##     on a given station's schema) would silently revert the whole
##     charts.json to stale content with only a journal entry to show for
##     it. Restored per-field #try/#except wrapping (falling back to []
##     -- matching the array shape .series().json normally returns) for
##     every hardware-dependent/optional field: particulates, air
##     density, cloud cover, ET, greenhouse gases, lightning, pollen,
##     vpd, and solar/UV. barometer, base rain, outTemp/dewpoint/
##     humidity, and wind are genuinely universal wview_extended schema
##     types and are left unguarded, per that same convention.
##  3. Also found and fixed while verifying JSON well-formedness: the
##     tail of this file had one extra, unmatched closing '}' (3 '{' vs
##     4 '}' in the original) -- silently produced invalid JSON on every
##     successful generation, independent of bugs #1/#2 above. Removed.
##
